From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: [PATCH] shcore: store the whole path in SHRegSetPath

Purpose: show XP's icons for image files, and run the open commands XP's
picture viewer (shimgvw.dll) registers.
XP behavior: SHRegSetPath writes a file path to the registry; read back, it
is the path that was passed.
Wine before: SHRegSetPathA and SHRegSetPathW passed the path's length in
characters as the data's size in bytes, without the terminator. The W form
stored half the path: shimgvw's DllRegisterServer left the image types with
DefaultIcon "shimgv" (for "shimgvw.dll,1"), so .jpg, .png, .bmp and .gif
files had the unknown file's icon, and its commands ended at
"...\system32\shimgvw.dl".
Change: both pass the size in bytes, with the terminator.
Evidence: a +reg trace of regsvr32 registering XP's shimgvw.dll shows
SHRegSetPathW writing L"shimgvw.dll,1" followed by NtSetValueKey with 13
bytes. tests/shreg-set-path.c fails before and prints PASS with the change.
Scope: every caller. Environment strings are still not put back into the
path (Wine's FIXME).
---
 dlls/shcore/main.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/dlls/shcore/main.c b/dlls/shcore/main.c
index 426a842..db60243 100644
--- a/dlls/shcore/main.c
+++ b/dlls/shcore/main.c
@@ -2348,7 +2348,7 @@ DWORD WINAPI SHRegSetPathA(HKEY hkey, const char *subkey, const char *value, con
 
     /* FIXME: PathUnExpandEnvStringsA() */
 
-    return SHSetValueA(hkey, subkey, value, REG_SZ, path, lstrlenA(path));
+    return SHSetValueA(hkey, subkey, value, REG_SZ, path, (lstrlenA(path) + 1) * sizeof(*path));
 }
 
 /*************************************************************************
@@ -2361,7 +2361,7 @@ DWORD WINAPI SHRegSetPathW(HKEY hkey, const WCHAR *subkey, const WCHAR *value, c
 
     /* FIXME: PathUnExpandEnvStringsW(); */
 
-    return SHSetValueW(hkey, subkey, value, REG_SZ, path, lstrlenW(path));
+    return SHSetValueW(hkey, subkey, value, REG_SZ, path, (lstrlenW(path) + 1) * sizeof(*path));
 }
 
 /*************************************************************************
